  "worked_solution": "We have $\\frac{1}{8}$ on the left and $\\frac{3}{8}$ on the right.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14129500/assets/abab6ca3b021dd1a8d38ea55008707c374f03e52b930fa3fa6dd187fe7945047.png)\n\nThe shape on the left has $1$ shaded piece, and the shape on the right has $3$ shaded pieces. So, the number of shaded pieces has increased by a factor of $3.$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{8}\\times 3=\\frac{3}{8}.\n$$\n\nSo, the missing number is $3.$",
